# Google Drive sync for the DESKTOP build. Optional: without it the app builds
# and runs exactly as before, the preload exposes no Drive bridge at all, and
# the card on /backup stays a description with nothing to click.
#
# This is the *Desktop app* OAuth client, which is a different client from the
# web app's — see docs/google-drive-sync.md. Unlike the web flow, this one does
# have a client secret.
#
# That secret is not confidential, and nothing here pretends otherwise: RFC 8252
# §8.5 says a credential shipped inside an installed application can be
# extracted by anyone, which is why PKCE — not the secret — is what protects the
# exchange, and why `drive.file` is what bounds the damage. It is kept out of
# the repo so that a fork is never quietly talking to someone else's Google
# project, not because hiding it would make it safe.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.desktop.local` (git-ignored) and fill it in.
# `npm run desktop:build` bakes these into the packaged app; an environment
# variable of the same name overrides the file.
MYTOME_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
MYTOME_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
